# A range by mouse and keys (3-E3a). `level` is x 0..200, y 0..20, 0..100
# by 1 at 20, with a 16 px thumb: a point x maps to (x - 8) / 184 of the
# range. `off` is disabled, at x 333..533.
#
# Shift with an arrow is left out: vapors steps by ten then (the
# 2026-10-27 direct-tools decision), Chromium by one.
listen pointerdown pointermove pointerup pointercancel gotpointercapture lostpointercapture click input change keydown focusin
click 100 10                  the middle of level: 50, pressed and released
expect event pointerdown input#level
expect event input input#level
expect event change input#level
expect event click input#level
expect focus input#level
expect value input#level 50
press 100 10                  a drag begins where the thumb is
expect event pointerdown input#level
move 150 10                   dragged right: 77
expect event pointermove input#level
expect event input input#level
expect value input#level 77
move 400 300                  off the input, still dragging: the end
expect event input input#level
expect value input#level 100
release 400 300               the drag ends with the change
expect event pointerup input#level
expect event change input#level
expect value input#level 100
key ArrowLeft                 one step down, with input and change
expect event keydown input#level
expect event input input#level
expect event change input#level
expect value input#level 99
key ArrowDown
expect value input#level 98
key ArrowRight
expect value input#level 99
key ArrowUp
expect value input#level 100
key PageDown                  a tenth of the range
expect value input#level 90
key PageUp
expect value input#level 100
key Home
expect value input#level 0
key End
expect value input#level 100
key Tab                       on to the next range
expect focus-visible input#plain
key ArrowRight                plain: 0..100 at 50
expect value input#plain 51
click 433 10                  off is disabled: no value, no focus
expect no event input
expect focus body
expect value input#off 50
touch-down 100 10             a finger on level takes the value where it lands
expect event pointerdown input#level
expect event input input#level
expect value input#level 50
touch-move 150 10             sideways, past the tap slop: it slides, owned by the range
expect event input input#level
expect value input#level 77
touch-up 150 10               the drag ends with the change
expect event pointerup input#level
expect event change input#level
touch-down 100 10             a finger again, 50
expect event input input#level
touch-move 100 60             down the page, past the slop: a scroll, so the pan cancels the touch
expect event pointercancel input#level
expect no event input
expect value input#level 50
touch-up 100 60               cancelled: no pointerup
expect no event pointerup
